Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:25:21 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 35/39] Metal diamond engine: UPML of the z slabs three
 components of a cell at a time (snapshot cg30i)

A z slab has one lane of a z-vector per cell, so it stays a loop over cells, but one pass now does the three
components: two index words per cell, the flux of the three components as one float4, and the coefficient sets as
one float4 for the voltages and one for the currents (OPENEMS_DIAMOND_PML3=0, or more than 65536 sets: a float at a
time). A third of the loop passes and about half the loads. The SMA launch, whose UPML is one z slab and costs 41 %
of the engine time, ran 7 % faster (paired rounds, loaded machine). diamond_check.sh 72 of 72 identical.

Generated-by: Claude Fable 5.2 (Anthropic)
Signed-off-by: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
